  "problem": "Consider the following initial value problem for the functions $y=y(x),z=z(x),w=w(x):$\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}=2x+z-w,\\, & y(0)=0 \\\\ {z}^{′}=xz+y,\\, & z(0)=1 \\\\ {w}^{′}=y-z+{w}^{2},\\, & w(0)=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe wish to approximate the solution using Euler's method.\nWhat entries should be placed in the columns for $Δy,$ $Δz,$ and $Δw$ in the table below if the step size is $Δx=1?$\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ | $w$ | ${w}^{′}$ | $Δw$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ |  |  | {{field-1}} |  |  | {{field-2}} |  |  | {{field-3}} |\n\nTherefore, $y(1)≈$\n{{field-4}},\n$z(1)≈$\n{{field-5}},\nand $w(1)≈$\n{{field-6}}.",
